[{"id":"VRCE-2-18-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":1,"english":"At this time Laksmana, sorely distressed, addressed the weeping Kausalyā, the mother of Rāma with the following words suitable to that occasion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ef2b989c0aa22cea3db5129d97520221cf4953d0a28bd1109796414622ff3a2b","compact":"ecd82853ce5b31305cdcaa911149b618fcbe8f228b2bc4b4567c94fc76ad6249","nasal":"010b1fe2ba7fb0b05e384a127afbbf1ca8d686ddf912bc1d8da9faf5823589f3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":2,"english":"I like it not, Oh worshipful one, that Räghava, should repair to the forest, renouncing this grandeur of sovereignty. The king is uxorious, old and therefore of perverted judgement and is addicted to worldly affairs; being under the influence of his wife and passion what could he not speak?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d45761eddf9fa8db1e07e67c3dc1d2f3bafc593a46c105231d608ba30202649a","compact":"837246497b6a536e84cbb0b01aa85111974790c9dadeb2bf49362ceeeeca6147","nasal":"837246497b6a536e84cbb0b01aa85111974790c9dadeb2bf49362ceeeeca6147"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":3,"english":"I like it not, Oh worshipful one, that Räghava, should repair to the forest, renouncing this grandeur of sovereignty. The king is uxorious, old and therefore of perverted judgement and is addicted to worldly affairs; being under the influence of his wife and passion what could he not speak?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8bf6c682af11046b97eeec0e0c402b4f2ff71d72cd68bc103826ff9cd16e9ec7","compact":"69e5b822a0567f34044cd14894f7f429574ed01d31df2ebae583ae7004d33c4c","nasal":"69e5b822a0567f34044cd14894f7f429574ed01d31df2ebae583ae7004d33c4c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":4,"english":"I do not see any such fault or sin in Rāma that he should be banished from the kingdom to range in the wood.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"85a59a2ef974df835fc5f8496b79c6a01cff979518f2b13fbbf9c7b975532078","compact":"73b70cbc421ed3cbc96cf16a73c96f653c4dc8bc9f7406f3df625a1169e5e680","nasal":"73b70cbc421ed3cbc96cf16a73c96f653c4dc8bc9f7406f3df625a1169e5e680"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":5,"english":"I do not find any such man in this world, even amongst great enemies, who, forsaken for heinous sins, can cite, even in his absence, any fault of him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7de2f52a537a89bba384bf2a0fd566aa0f405cdb118a8cc842ef6d1eb77ddebc","compact":"155e451abdd99d4d57a984f425104513b34d15eacf625b28b973c84440c8f6e2","nasal":"155e451abdd99d4d57a984f425104513b34d15eacf625b28b973c84440c8f6e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":6,"english":"Observing what law of righteousness does the monarch, without any cause, renounce such a son who is like to celestials, simple, well disciplined and beloved even of the enemies?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.844,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5b5f36831f46cbe5105c047282d37079d031b4d76e30814460b8ac195ae507b1","compact":"c79728250054204d665e9abd87e3ae311d35a12667c6ff0fe791dbf7c3afcb06","nasal":"6db4b69d07869db94a44de2aa59872d6d6a0730f8703b6433f3c3bc6fbef446a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":7,"english":"What son, remembering his father's conduct, shall carry in his heart these words of the king, who has again gone back to childhood?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"81fcd91d1a27963546800b4d03a13d7274595df79677f45972f3846c13301a49","compact":"bb7c90c37436ea753b42fd7b90343cf6863386cc5b6faa43c58ed4181d948c78","nasal":"bb7c90c37436ea753b42fd7b90343cf6863386cc5b6faa43c58ed4181d948c78"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":8,"english":"Ere people come to know this proposal of exile, do you secure the government of the kingdom to yourself with me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5cd3a2c4a3fa95a066d14697691f7b05b3c9614cbbded2eb8282dbec756cc525","compact":"cce622de56cd30b4af75ea01ec8010d218abdb05af8fd4934f5d2a0fcb2bedf2","nasal":"cce622de56cd30b4af75ea01ec8010d218abdb05af8fd4934f5d2a0fcb2bedf2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":9,"english":"Who can disturb the installation, Oh Rāghava, myself protecting you by your side with my bows, like to Death himself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9b7a8e6dae210acc582cbe3fe6e41908353d1cb099e2cf30557c123088eebc8a","compact":"8cabd100d4a4ea4001891596caad3f982be57c5ba062b81d3f5bf26091319da9","nasal":"a2a5b0f239a935abfd04d953dd10f9320f3287eb05195ae9723a0e8ef694d42b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":10,"english":"If any body stands here as an enemy, surely shall I, Oh best of men, depopulate the whole city of Ayodhyā with sharp arrows.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c2fdaa081aba2b79d72cf1db17e3aa87053b82ed58874415432909b103c71ffc","compact":"bed750c5d95c2afa8b450b81073fe49ae2bda5f71d63b6f32955dec629099097","nasal":"bed750c5d95c2afa8b450b81073fe49ae2bda5f71d63b6f32955dec629099097"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":11,"english":"I shall immolate all who shall stand by Bharata or wish him well, certainly mildness brings about discomfiture.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.794,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a5f82cfdcbb7cccf21ca24ae73fafc78ec7af385bc06eb23711bed5693d205af","compact":"1f28fdba480ab7032b247e88ad3ffb579c140ab488ae6440101a7855c9647373","nasal":"1f28fdba480ab7032b247e88ad3ffb579c140ab488ae6440101a7855c9647373"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":12,"english":"Who dares conferring on on Bharata the kingdom, carrying hostility with me and you?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.741,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"652dfee3035818ace918c85da3a85cf0d4633c05528d617dd14c6beba8fd0a05","compact":"6e79410c3d4f1dd483fb40c7947c8bbd0fbd2aadfadcdc3761f4b590aa1cd83f","nasal":"6e79410c3d4f1dd483fb40c7947c8bbd0fbd2aadfadcdc3761f4b590aa1cd83f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":13,"english":"Oh worshipful one, verily am I attached at heart to my brother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"386ec61c33ed6751d6d3ba402a6bdc8de95c30c86de683adb1a329a91f5cb731","compact":"d336ae20b0376d5218ac56d386f7120ee14f217bf93bdb89883794acbae38880","nasal":"d336ae20b0376d5218ac56d386f7120ee14f217bf93bdb89883794acbae38880"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":14,"english":"By truth, bow, gifts and things dear to me, do I swear to you; if Rāma shall enter into the wood, know me, Oh worshipful one, to have entered into the fire before that.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9ec5a977f12a2a479f5e0cc7c7a7cde0a0b5e66e6407d3d0d7bdd0e5f682dfc1","compact":"97616775a400aa30f80fafdb370a17529ee0269c75fca871cdc87d6308f6d8ee","nasal":"97616775a400aa30f80fafdb370a17529ee0269c75fca871cdc87d6308f6d8ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":15,"english":"Like to the sun dispelling darkness, shall I remove your sorrow by dint of my power; may your worshipful self and Rāghava witness it. Readily shall I despatch my father, whose heart is unduly attached to Kaikeyſ and who is therefore vile and being old contemptibly playing the child.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3fcd003b9c76945b6a8c218589b362ae477e8ae6b35861975019bb2da7b78209","compact":"48f42dd1022d331f403a878e105b53560328b04da65af10b8dcd6dbaf3b8182a","nasal":"48f42dd1022d331f403a878e105b53560328b04da65af10b8dcd6dbaf3b8182a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":16,"english":"Hearing these words of the high-souled Laks maņa, Kausaly, weeping and being pressed with sorrow spoke these words to Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.847,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21ba370f65b66be3a5caaaf1a1aebcb3a3518fa8ee503a132fd2935e158daf65","compact":"11b0e29c49e2d80dabf3efe58a43253b2508343a75a3f11866d700f8f951702b","nasal":"f99689d76e0f4d96e1df69d38babb99a85d381469d8b8fdcb5fbf39fec39c412"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":17,"english":"You have heard, Oh my son, what your brother Laksmana said; and if you like, do what seems reasonable to you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b0f84a456ab93709a05f7cbb9704ddb804ac68a37fdc1642534721026154e430","compact":"7e3f86b4d203e86cc173c3ef4777ce92e4047ae26240e04229fc7516be504d0d","nasal":"2b208b8a1295d8b2d37ecfec609309e4a60eb2f70e90beccec9ae705679b7a81"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":18,"english":"It does not behove you, hearing the sinful words given vent to by the co-wife, to repair hence, leaving me who is sore distressed with sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"73cda7d9e3452924d4a8e46d08af44dd420e1786e277c2b7276d64a4bf5350ac","compact":"cc9ace70cfc186e1bad906496da78b4b29c2ce6cd145f6994c7265c1b158817e","nasal":"507b176f62e1b08f34c2e839ffb90da806bc642a988b98274a68a9491ffc1242"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":19,"english":"Oh you pious one, having knowledge of religion, if do you wish to acquire righteousness, serve me here and continue practising the best of all virtues.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da5ebd93c744ee91ab93cfcef456079d459ab71ef98a3ccd7280cce697fb8fb1","compact":"4170cc53b2dc452943f3049117006da303c9eb0663b3b298fb4f886cc853a235","nasal":"4170cc53b2dc452943f3049117006da303c9eb0663b3b298fb4f886cc853a235"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":20,"english":"Hear, Oh my son, the great ascetic Kasyapa, lived in his house, serving his mother continually and being crowned with best moral merit reached heaven.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1ffafacdc0926650c82b905478f0849f20d2fc26d6380ad444d6483b4de4b3ef","compact":"d008e73ce84a78d4ef0914acad140796516bb84807839a2b3f811c2cdcef0037","nasal":"d008e73ce84a78d4ef0914acad140796516bb84807839a2b3f811c2cdcef0037"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":21,"english":"As the monarch is worshipful to you in veneration so am I. I do not permit you, to repair hence to the forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"abc5ca01fdb0b7143e4bf7f527b1208b486b7a59d32732d49f1c2ab34aa91aaf","compact":"52dddb3ae3b657f2721bf28f36f72d0e09da901ae796a8f27b0ace9d7a29c07b","nasal":"42528b614dfa71131f087aa745b2ef87128fecc1655c8b2e61b7bde5ac868062"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":22,"english":"Separated from you I do not need life or happiness; with you I would prefer faring on grass.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.508,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e551b145ed081de717e575fa102aaf167168f2bcd25bc40c6370baf35e27bffb","compact":"f4c5e993499ad6b724b57e38b0d49b433e845f0840397f6e00ada88a7ec89e5f","nasal":"536c709504e78abe8f894ea494ca56185c39814580a16040cfaffee2f9a1e24e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":23,"english":"If do you depart to the forest leaving me troubled with sorrow, I shall resort to the vow of fasting and shall not be able to sustain my life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dfa16405fc7d4a0af588cc29a320bc55121e5a8317baa5a21d39d6e88a5e64f2","compact":"8b8661b00e727bcd257d5a9ddd16b51fdfb0ecc1fdac7ca87bf7327b1ff2016e","nasal":"8b8661b00e727bcd257d5a9ddd16b51fdfb0ecc1fdac7ca87bf7327b1ff2016e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":24,"english":"And then you shall receive the penalty of hell, well-known to the people, as did the ocean, the lord of rivers, for like unrighteousness, suffer the agony of Brahmanicide\".* *The text has been here a little freely translated to make it compatible with the legend to which it refers. The ocean, thus goes the story, caused the grief of his mother. Upon which, Maharși Pippalāda, through magical power, subjected him to agony of hell. This agony the mother of Rāma relates as the same that follows the sin of Brahminicide.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.89,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"47135d08054f9f9928b1f48014bd04d029221a0b61fe652e559cd57a5a0156db","compact":"dbd3f1effa16d76910477678c731887417ad2464ac594d3bb711df2b8459167b","nasal":"ef5a74459eb1ee8a369fad7d74c364b91189576a66acb4d2eb7a8f9a98c9d328"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-25","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":25,"english":"Whereupon to his mother Kausalyä, sorrowful and weeping, spoke Răma, virtuous-souled these words of righteousness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"02c5ec070a5dba1578c31899b80c02e8272b73be7ec00be5eaa18383da5749f9","compact":"002bb9da4437bb19776b09474c2678f59329a7c819ecb26168d4441652432b40","nasal":"574b152628f9797793c355b2efa6f2d27e4bd4fb2d0fe710f4480452f38d0ed0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-26","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":26,"english":"There is no power in me to transgress my father's behest's; bend low I my head to you, I want to proceed to the forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018026","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"920a9db7e0e71137f89e00ddf6d93ac0916d566973aae4211f620c6164960d2c","compact":"03656464871219a6b31eed072430f8f3acedb6473abe2beda8037db93810cced","nasal":"656a69ffc43fdbfb227d84b0b74de88dd4904f8d293014cf7bee17b366a41c2b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-27","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":27,"english":"The learned Rși Kandu, who lived in the forest keeping the word of his father, killed a cow, knowing it to be unrighteousness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018027","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a9feeb09a01872b037486ea4d9a004aa5c07348a7459e091b04590549c7a48e7","compact":"a1ce9a9dd9af8e055b6669be68844415c707a92ba7268abb181a9e9cbd0ce335","nasal":"4441c2be7b73db9a41c2a499a705f3e14fdec27359768536c82bfa4aa1cd3986"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-28","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":28,"english":"In our line the descendants of Sagara, at the command of their father, met with signal destruction, while digging the earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.619,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-30"],"status"