by worthies gone before. Surely shall I accomplish that which is worthy of being performed in this world and nothing else, one going by his father's behest's is not certainly degraded.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6ce06e2510e58d267919a2a72c5dffb8fac6c97fef1accbc9bb67340494d7a64","compact":"dcbdb5a71b5bf8cd75318e20987c47df2b9c49cc9745f2fe5bca7bb5b15ce5ff","nasal":"79f3e8c424c3088e451a8db340234d933ae804941ae3644d7ed787cc742b403c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-32","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":32,"english":"I know full well, Oh, Laksmana, your affection towards me and your power, strength • and unconquerable force.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.272,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"995d31a1cf296d64c1855b24d9e8204358d5401a096f38841e094af5176049a7","compact":"44632a360bf1a711b45a7f42d46d4f1ea2ff1ee0e1fc254326b03769c4aa6033","nasal":"44632a360bf1a711b45a7f42d46d4f1ea2ff1ee0e1fc254326b03769c4aa6033"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":33,"english":"Righteousness is the prime object in this world and in righteousness is established truth, and this excellent utterance of my father is in keeping with righteousness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.812,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f30001ac58a583c4ea4f9bb8175fdc039ddbd674119c4618d6abd7357653cca7","compact":"e6ce7cb051a306568a438b885258d6e90b03debca1cb7a84541587f41a814b09","nasal":"e6ce7cb051a306568a438b885258d6e90b03debca1cb7a84541587f41a814b09"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-34","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":34,"english":"It does not become them, O hero, who abide in righteousness to fail to carry out the commands of father, mother or a Brahmin.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018034","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2f7c4052e817c44d0f52b4b690a0da41dd1dd677e62196153288aa6588d780f4","compact":"e090d16c51f382427aaefacdf1ef47f38673a93cd939843f1ab310b609154dea","nasal":"e090d16c51f382427aaefacdf1ef47f38673a93cd939843f1ab310b609154dea"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-35","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":35,"english":"While I have been, Oh warrior, ordered by Kaikeyi at my father's words, I shall not be able to transgress those behest's again.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.848,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018035","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a5cbf66ee0b738a1e805e5f9eba32ec985247fcb14d0908e8ad3f0f4fdd73619","compact":"2ac159e015a5423fb8a4c1d510786141268ce8658d1c7427feb9e1b335b09bf5","nasal":"5e921ea5e6c3c3acc869e378f889d40ac27f9655f70871010e5d0cd06498ca82"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-36","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":36,"english":"Do you relinquish therefore this unrighteous purpose of your consequent to the virtues of the Kșatriyas; do you abide by righteousness but not cruelty, and follow my decision.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.844,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018036","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3819bdb2e4995c088a2dfcf882db4b6bd59ccbd2dc20b3794a0014a7435c1233","compact":"f40e7888adae93633ef51a3d9ee1839e4e19cfd260d4babbd8c1a23e34fb79d6","nasal":"f40e7888adae93633ef51a3d9ee1839e4e19cfd260d4babbd8c1a23e34fb79d6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-37","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":37,"english":"Saying these words to Lakşmaņa out of fraternal affection, spoke again Rāma to Kausalyā with clasped hands and with his head bending low.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018037","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cbcb5b69f5c63697f4ea273e81d012c59bb1da1e60b39daa877e4ce57107b054","compact":"65c8e8d9a6a38dcc7945092f4f32e98c04d83f5a29160c458e1554bd7c13dc40","nasal":"684d2d57099c30d12353c9794c1b915f6c2be8d3450e6e2e719196fc5deb0a04"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-38","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":38,"english":"I do bind you with an oath of my life, Oh venerable one, to allow me to wander away hence into the wood. Do you perform benedictory ceremonies for my welfare. Like to the royal saint Yayāti, in the days of yore once falling on earth going again to the abode of celestials, I shall, fulfilling my vows, again return home from the forest.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.606,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-44","DUTT-2-21-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018038","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6b0f750d1c0f618db8e41d5b86f391f4f830efa755b40c39c0faf0a23331fde2","compact":"3d770fec55713e6e049cfe7e2bd2d89f5cf5f6deb2c9865ad2761957c1e85076","nasal":"c06fbd249515cb52195762ce2dd1e6cea0303bfc01e857d1a164b179ff1bb2b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-39","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":39,"english":"I cannot neglect eminent fame being impelled by avarice for kingdom alone. Life is but of short duration, Oh worshipful one, and as such I do not long for acquiring this nether earth by means unrighteous.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.702,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-60"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018039","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c7d308cf03486ad5d028bb1858fb1b5a8183a9d88459e5acfcbdf7540ef78277","compact":"a7673acd49f46a5d96d2459f04a73ae01a2034359e4f84c202e4a385719f36f3","nasal":"e10adde6802a5bc1cc38f0d1eb50a3935073c7bc6677098c74b7f7bf979c57c9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-18-40","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":18,"verse":40,"english":"Rāma, that foremost of men, with a view to range into the forest Dandaka after patiently propitiating his mother and instructing fully his younger brother the mysteries of righteousness, went round his mother with reverence and made up his mind to repair to the forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-21-61"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2018040","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0cd032575e7c375ae430799ee4921e7309cfab6f7f137d4f00904c15db747495","compact":"521a2149b1b69a2c331eb89bd19209f6bb64eac9ba05678cd573c974742bf506","nasal":"6da0cd414aedd10e1fd2c57bf616ebb79eeb73b39a246584034478fac807704b"}}]
